  "tiktok": {
    "caption": "ADHD mom confession: 4 planners this year, same task on page 1 of every one 🫠\n\nplanners tell me what to do. they never helped me start. what finally worked: making step 1 easier than washing a dish.\n\nhow many planners are you on? 👇\nsave this for your next drop-off 📌\n\nthe app on the last slides is FOCO, link in bio 💜",
    "hashtags": [
      "#adhdmom",
      "#adhdplanner",
      "#taskparalysis",
      "#adhdtiktok"
    ]
  },
  "instagram": {
    "caption": "ADHD planner confession: 4 planners this year, and the same task sits on page 1 of every one.\n\nI'm not lazy. Washing a dish is easy to start. \"Write the newsletter\" isn't, and no planner ever changed that.\n\n1. 9:10, daycare drop-off, 3 hours for one job\n2. I went to wash one dish... and cleaned the whole kitchen\n3. 11:20, my client emails, pickup is at 12:30\n4. I snapped my planner page with FOCO. One tap broke the newsletter into tiny steps, and I did only step 1\n\n12:14, first draft done.\n\nSave this, and send it to the mom friend with a planner collection.\n\n💜 The app I use is FOCO, link in bio.",
    "hashtags": [
      "#adhdmom",
      "#adhdplanner",
      "#taskparalysis",
      "#adhdwomen"
    ],
    "altText": "Story-style video of a mom working from home during daycare hours: four planners with the same task on page one, a kitchen she cleaned instead, a client email, then she scans her planner page with FOCO, the task lands in her day, one tap breaks it into tiny steps, and she starts with FOCO's focus timer and finishes a first draft before pickup."
